{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_zgpmcsxbpo5zaiw2ixuatfepyiywlecxmcquo52dcih73zrofkaa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All four files read. Findings below; all line refs are into `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-Qil4GP/c_src/src/`.\n\n# 1. `pcre2_match()` — `pcre2_match.c:6972-8246`\n\n**Argument / option validation (in exact order, 7038-7120)**\n- `subject == NULL && length == 0` → substituted with an internal 1-unit dummy buffer (`null_str`), treated as valid empty subject (7038).\n- `match_data == NULL` → `PCRE2_ERROR_NULL` (only case where `match_data->rc` is *not* set).\n- `code == NULL || subject == NULL` (subject NULL with length != 0) → `ERROR_NULL`, stored in `match_data->rc`.\n- `options & ~PUBLIC_MATCH_OPTIONS` → `ERROR_BADOPTION`. Valid match-time options (71-75): ANCHORED, ENDANCHORED, NOTBOL, NOTEOL, NOTEMPTY, NOTEMPTY_ATSTART, NO_UTF_CHECK, PARTIAL_HARD, PARTIAL_SOFT, NO_JIT, COPY_MATCHED_SUBJECT, DISABLE_RECURSELOOP_CHECK.\n- `length == PCRE2_ZERO_TERMINATED` → length computed by `strlen` (7050).\n- `start_offset > length` → `ERROR_BADOFFSET`. `start_offset == length` is legal (start at end of subject).\n- `re->magic_number != MAGIC_NUMBER` → `ERROR_BADMAGIC`; `(re->flags & PCRE2_MODE_MASK) != width/8` → `ERROR_BADMODE`.\n- Pattern flags `PCRE2_NOTEMPTY_SET` / `PCRE2_NE_ATST_SET` (from `(*NOTEMPTY)` / `(*NOTEMPTY_ATSTART)` in the pattern) are OR-ed into `options` by bit arithmetic (7080-7084) → equivalent to caller passing the option.\n- `mb->partial = 2` if PARTIAL_HARD, else `1` if PARTIAL_SOFT, else `0` (PARTIAL_HARD wins when both set) (7105).\n- `mb->partial != 0 && ((re->overall_options|options) & PCRE2_ENDANCHORED)` → `ERROR_BADOPTION` (compile-time *or* match-time ENDANCHORED).\n- `mcontext != NULL && mcontext->offset_limit != PCRE2_UNSET && !(re->overall_options & PCRE2_USE_OFFSET_LIMIT)` → `ERROR_BADOFFSETLIMIT`. Valid combos: no context / offset_limit UNSET (any pattern); offset_limit set + pattern compiled with USE_OFFSET_LIMIT.\n- Reuse across calls: if `match_data->flags & PCRE2_MD_COPIED_SUBJECT`, the previously copied subject is freed and the flag cleared (7126-7131); then `match_data->subject = NULL`, `match_data->startchar = 0`.\n\n**JIT path (7148-7242)** — taken only if `re->executable_jit != NULL && (options & ~PUBLIC_JIT_MATCH_OPTIONS) == 0` (i.e. ANCHORED/ENDANCHORED/NO_JIT/DISABLE_RECURSELOOP_CHECK at match time force the interpreter). Falls through to interpreter if `pcre2_jit_match` returns `ERROR_JIT_BADOPTION`. On JIT success with COPY_MATCHED_SUBJECT it mallocs+memcpy (NULL subject if `length==0`), else restores `original_subject`.\n\n**UTF checking (7269-7385)** — branch matrix: `utf` (pattern PCRE2_UTF) × `NO_UTF_CHECK` × `allow_invalid` (pattern PCRE2_MATCH_INVALID_UTF).\n- Check runs when `utf && (!NO_UTF_CHECK || allow_invalid)` — MATCH_INVALID_UTF forces a check even with NO_UTF_CHECK.\n- 8/16-bit, `!allow_invalid`, `*start_match` not a first code unit: `start_offset > 0` → `ERROR_BADUTFOFFSET`; `start_offset == 0` → `ERROR_UTF8_ERR20` / `ERROR_UTF16_ERR3`.\n- 8/16-bit `allow_invalid`: bad start units are skipped forward (`skipped_bad_start`), which suppresses the lookbehind rewind.\n- `mb->check_subject` = start_match rewound by `re->max_lookbehind` *characters* (32-bit: clamped at subject if `start_offset < max_lookbehind`); with no UTF check, `check_subject == subject` (lookbehind may reach subject start).\n- `valid_utf` failure: `!allow_invalid || rc > 0` → return the UTF error with `match_data->startchar` = absolute offset. With `allow_invalid` and `rc < 0`: fragment matching — `end_subject` truncated at the bad unit; if the bad unit is *before* start_match, skip it and retry with the true end; else `fragment_options = PCRE2_NOTEOL`.\n- Fragment loop after ENDLOOP (8109-8163): on NOMATCH/PARTIAL with `end_subject != true_end_subject`, restart at next valid fragment with `fragment_options = NOTBOL` (rest valid) or `NOTBOL|NOTEOL` (another error follows); at true end, PARTIAL is downgraded to NOMATCH.\n\n**Context/limits (7390-7546)**\n- `mcontext == NULL` → default match context, memctl from the *pattern*; else memctl from context.\n- Each of match/depth/heap limit = `min(context value, pattern (*LIMIT_xxx) value)` (7502-7509).\n- `frame_size = align(offsetof(heapframe,ovector) + 2*top_bracket*sizeof(PCRE2_SIZE))`; `heapframes_size = max(10*frame_size, START_FRAMES_SIZE)`; if `heapframes_size/1024 > heap_limit`: clamp to `1024*heap_limit`, and if that is `< frame_size` → `ERROR_HEAPLIMIT` before matching starts.\n- Frame vector reused if `match_data->heapframes_size >= heapframes_size`, else freed + re-malloc'd (`NULL` → `ERROR_NOMEMORY`, `heapframes_size` reset to 0). First frame's ovector is memset to 0xff.\n- Runtime growth (750-803): doubling, capped by heap limit; `ERROR_HEAPLIMIT` when the cap leaves less than one frame; `PCRE2_SIZE_MAX` edge cases → `ERROR_NOMEMORY`.\n- Per-frame checks (873-874): `mb->match_call_count++ >= match_limit` → `ERROR_MATCHLIMIT`; `Frdepth >= match_limit_depth` → `ERROR_DEPTHLIMIT`.\n\n**Start optimizations (7554-7944)** — gated as a whole by `re->optimization_flags & PCRE2_OPTIM_START_OPTIMIZE` (cleared by `PCRE2_NO_START_OPTIMIZE`/`(*NO_START_OPT)`); when disabled every start position is tried and all callouts fire.\n- first code unit: `PCRE2_FIRSTSET` → `has_first_cu`, `first_cu2 = fcc[first_cu]` if `PCRE2_FIRSTCASELESS`; for cu > 127, `UCD_OTHERCASE` used when (8-bit) `ucp && !utf`, or (16/32-bit) `utf || ucp` (7557-7572).\n- start bitmap used only when `!FIRSTSET && !startline && PCRE2_FIRSTMAPSET` (7574).\n- req code unit: `PCRE2_LASTSET` (+`PCRE2_LASTCASELESS`, same UCD rules) (7579-7594).\n- `anchored = (re->overall_options|options) & PCRE2_ANCHORED`; `firstline = !anchored && (re->overall_options & PCRE2_FIRSTLINE)`; `startline = re->flags & PCRE2_STARTLINE`; `bumpalong_limit = offset_limit==UNSET ? true_end : subject+offset_limit` (7397-7401).\n- FIRSTLINE: `end_subject` temporarily moved to the first newline at/after start (UTF-aware scan), restored at 7843; failing at that newline breaks the loop (8051).\n- anchored + (first_cu or bitmap): single test of `*start_match` (also requires `start_match < end_subject`) → NOMATCH if it fails.\n- unanchored, has_first_cu: caseless vs caseful; 8-bit uses `memchr` with the `memchr_found_first_cu/2` caching (reset per fragment at 7609-7612); 16/32-bit inline loop. If not found and `mb->partial == 0 && start_match >= mb->end_subject` → NOMATCH break; with partial != 0 (or FIRSTLINE-truncated end) one more cycle runs at end.\n- unanchored, no first_cu, `startline`: skip forward to just after a newline (only when `start_match > subject+start_offset`), plus CR→LF extra bump for ANY/ANYCRLF.\n- unanchored, no first_cu, not startline, bitmap: scan; units > 255 map to bit 255 in 16/32-bit; same partial/end condition.\n- minlength and req_cu tests both disabled when `mb->partial != 0` (7847).\n  - `end_subject - start_match < re->minlength` → NOMATCH.\n  - req_cu search starts at `start_match + (has_first_cu?1:0)`, only if `p > req_cu_ptr`; skipped entirely when `check_length >= REQ_CU_MAX` (anchored) or `>= REQ_CU_MAX*1000` (unanchored); not found → NOMATCH; found → `req_cu_ptr` cached across bumpalong.\n- `start_match > bumpalong_limit` → NOMATCH (offset_limit semantics; limit is a *start* offset, inclusive).\n\n**Bumpalong loop / verb results (7959-8080)**\n- Per attempt: `cb.start_match` updated, `PCRE2_CALLOUT_STARTMATCH` flag set, `start_used_ptr = last_used_ptr = start_match`, `moptions = options|fragment_options`, `match_call_count = 0`, `end_offset_top = 0`, `skip_arg_count = 0`; `mb->mark = NULL` at the end of each failed attempt (nomatch_mark is *not* reset).\n- `MATCH_SKIP_ARG` (a `(*SKIP:NAME)` whose NAME was never marked): retry at the *same* position with `ignore_skip_arg = skip_arg_count`.\n- `MATCH_SKIP`: restart at `mb->verb_skip_ptr` if `> start_match`, otherwise treated as NOMATCH.\n- `MATCH_NOMATCH` / `MATCH_PRUNE` / `MATCH_THEN`: advance one character (UTF-aware), `ignore_skip_arg = 0`.\n- `MATCH_COMMIT`: `rc = NOMATCH` and the bumpalong loop is abandoned (no further start positions).\n- Anything else (MATCH_MATCH, PARTIAL, errors) exits.\n- Loop exits: `anchored`, `start_match > end_subject`, FIRSTLINE newline; CR/LF skip requires `start_match > subject+start_offset && start_match[-1]==CR && *start_match==LF && !(re->flags & PCRE2_HASCRORLF) && (nltype ANY|ANYCRLF || nllen==2)`.\n\n**Inside `match()` — options-sensitive behaviour**\n- NOTEMPTY / NOTEMPTY_ATSTART at OP_END/OP_ACCEPT (983-992): empty match rejected if NOTEMPTY, or if NOTEMPTY_ATSTART *and* `Fstart_match == start_subject + start_offset`; backtracking continues to look for a non-empty match.\n- ENDANCHORED (999-1014): `Feptr < end_subject` → NOMATCH; at OP_END it backtracks, after `(*ACCEPT)` it fails the whole attempt at this position (`return`, no backtracking).\n- \\K (`OP_SET_SOM` at 6689) can move `Fstart_match`; if it ends up `< start_subject+start_offset` or `> Feptr`, the match is rejected with `PCRE2_ERROR_BAD_BACKSLASH_K` unless the pattern was compiled with `PCRE2_EXTRA_ALLOW_LOOKAROUND_BSK` (`mb->allowlookaroundbsk`, 1022-1031).\n- NOTBOL: `^`/`\\A` (OP_CIRC 6570) fails at `start_subject`; OP_CIRCM at 6638. NOTEOL: `$` (OP_DOLL 6585) fails outright; without NOTEOL, `$` matches before a final newline unless the pattern has `PCRE2_DOLLAR_ENDONLY` (`mb->poptions`, 6586) — DOLLAR_ENDONLY is a *compile* option read at match time. Note 5934: NOTEOL is cleared inside lookaheads/other constructs.\n- DISABLE_RECURSELOOP_CHECK (5718-5734): without it, re-entering the same recursion group at the same `Feptr` and same `last_used_ptr` → `PCRE2_ERROR_RECURSELOOP`; with it, such loops instead terminate via match/heap limits.\n- Verbs: `(*MARK:X)`/`(*THEN:X)`/`(*PRUNE:X)`/`(*COMMIT:X)` set `Fmark = mb->nomatch_mark`; `(*SKIP:X)` deliberately does **not** set nomatch_mark (6836-6861). `(*FAIL)` → NOMATCH. Verbs inside a recursion cannot escape it (5751+).\n- mark reporting: on MATCH_MATCH `match_data->mark = mb->mark` (last successful mark); on NOMATCH/PARTIAL/error `match_data->mark = mb->nomatch_mark` (8169, 8211).\n\n**Result / ovector semantics (8166-8245)**\n- Always set: `code`, `mark`, `matchedby = PCRE2_MATCHEDBY_INTERPRETER`, `options = original_options` (the caller's options, not the NOTEMPTY-augmented ones).\n- Success: `rc = (end_offset_top >= 2*oveccount) ? 0 : end_offset_top/2 + 1` — so **rc == 0 means \"ovector too small\"** while ovector[0..2*oveccount-1] hold what fit. `ovector[0]/[1]` always written in `match()` (1045-1046); copy of frame ovector limited to `min(oveccount, top_bracket+1)` pairs (1050-1052); trailing pairs above `Foffset_top` set to `PCRE2_UNSET` (1053). `oveccount` is >= 1 always (`pcre2_match_data.c:57` clamps 0→1, >UINT16_MAX→UINT16_MAX), so ovector sizes to test: 1 (only whole match), `< top_bracket+1` (rc 0), exactly `top_bracket+1`, oversized (extra pairs untouched).\n- Also set on success: `subject_length`, `start_offset`, `startchar` (= start_match), `leftchar` (= start_used_ptr), `rightchar` (= max(last_used_ptr, end_match_ptr)).\n- COPY_MATCHED_SUBJECT on success: malloc+memcpy `length` units and set `PCRE2_MD_COPIED_SUBJECT`; `length == 0` → `subject = NULL` with the flag still set; malloc failure → `ERROR_NOMEMORY`. Without it, `subject = original_subject` (the caller's pointer, or the internal null_str for the NULL/0 case).\n- Partial: reported only if `match_partial != NULL` (i.e. `mb->hitend` was seen); `rc = PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL`, `ovector[0] = match_partial`, `ovector[1] = end_subject`, leftchar = `start_partial`. PARTIAL_SOFT keeps searching for a complete match (final rc from `match()` is NOMATCH but the recorded partial is returned); PARTIAL_HARD returns as soon as the end is hit. `mb->allowemptypartial` (= `max_lookbehind > 0 || PCRE2_MATCH_EMPTY`) allows an empty partial.\n- Errors other than NOMATCH/PARTIAL are returned verbatim and stored in `match_data->rc`; `match_data->subject` stays NULL for them.\n- Callouts (`do_callout`, 268-330): no-op returning 0 when `mcontext->callout == NULL`; cb version 2; `capture_top = Foffset_top/2+1`; `cb->offset_vector` is the frame ovector minus 2 with the first pair temporarily `PCRE2_UNSET`; `cb->mark = nomatch_mark`; `callout_flags` carries STARTMATCH/BACKTRACK (6913) and is cleared after each call. Return >0 → NOMATCH for that path, <0 → abandon with that error.\n\n# 2. `pcre2_dfa_match()` — `pcre2_dfa_match.c:3339-4126`\n\n**Validation order (3392-3459)**\n- Same NULL/length-0 subject substitution; `match_data == NULL` → ERROR_NULL (rc not stored); `code == NULL || subject == NULL || workspace == NULL` → ERROR_NULL.\n- `options & ~PUBLIC_DFA_MATCH_OPTIONS` → BADOPTION. Valid DFA options (83-87): ANCHORED, ENDANCHORED, NOTBOL, NOTEOL, NOTEMPTY, NOTEMPTY_ATSTART, NO_UTF_CHECK, PARTIAL_HARD, PARTIAL_SOFT, DFA_SHORTEST, DFA_RESTART, COPY_MATCHED_SUBJECT. (No ANCHORED-at-compile exclusion; no NO_JIT/COPY-only quirks; DISABLE_RECURSELOOP_CHECK is **not** accepted.)\n- `wscount < 20` → `ERROR_DFA_WSSIZE` (so minimum workspace is exactly 20 ints; test 19 / 20 / large).\n- `start_offset > length` → BADOFFSET.\n- partial + ENDANCHORED (compile or match) → BADOPTION.\n- pattern compiled with `PCRE2_MATCH_INVALID_UTF` → `ERROR_DFA_UINVALID_UTF` (always, regardless of subject).\n- BADMAGIC / BADMODE as in `pcre2_match`.\n- `(*NOTEMPTY)`/`(*NOTEMPTY_ATSTART)` pattern flags folded into options (3445-3449).\n- `DFA_RESTART`: requires `(workspace[0] & ~1) == 0 && workspace[1] >= 1 && workspace[1] <= (wscount-2)/INTS_PER_STATEBLOCK`, else `ERROR_DFA_BADRESTART`. DFA_RESTART also forces `anchored = TRUE` (3467) and disables *all* start optimizations (3708-3709).\n- `anchored = ANCHORED (match) || DFA_RESTART || ANCHORED (compile)`; `firstline`, `startline`, `bumpalong_limit` as in `pcre2_match` but offset-limit check happens only inside the `mcontext != NULL` branch (3503-3508); with `mcontext == NULL`, callout is NULL and limits come from `PRIV(default_match_context)`, then clamped by pattern limits (3517-3524).\n- UTF check (3589-3627): only when `utf && !NO_UTF_CHECK`; `start_offset > 0` triggers the mid-character check (`BADUTFOFFSET`) and the max_lookbehind rewind; no invalid-UTF tolerance.\n- Same first_cu / bitmap / req_cu / minlength / FIRSTLINE / startline optimizations as `pcre2_match` (3630-4013), gated additionally on `!DFA_RESTART`; partial (HARD or SOFT) disables the minlength and req_cu tests.\n\n**`internal_dfa_match` (529-3311)**\n- `mb->match_call_count++ >= match_limit` → MATCHLIMIT; `rlevel++ > match_limit_depth` → DEPTHLIMIT (depth counts nested *function* recursions, not characters).\n- `offsetcount &= ~1` (rounded down to even); workspace split: `wscount -= 2` then divided into two state vectors of `(wscount - wscount % (2*INTS_PER_STATEBLOCK)) / (2*INTS_PER_STATEBLOCK)` states — exceeding it in ADD_ACTIVE/ADD_NEW returns `ERROR_DFA_WSSIZE` at runtime (489-525), so \"too small but >= 20\" is a distinct testable case.\n- Match recording at the end ket (861-894): a match is recorded unless it is empty and forbidden by NOTEMPTY / (NOTEMPTY_ATSTART && at `start_subject+start_offset`). **Ordering: longest first** — new (longer) matches are memmove'd to the front of `offsets`; `match_count` grows; if `++match_count*2 > offsetcount` then `match_count = 0` (ovector overflow, longest matches retained → return value 0). `DFA_SHORTEST` returns immediately on the first match found (shortest).\n- Partial (3274-3295): only when no new states remain and `could_continue`, and either PARTIAL_HARD, or PARTIAL_SOFT with `match_count < 0`; plus (partial_newline, or at end of subject with either `ptr > start_used_ptr` or `mb->allowemptypartial`). Result `PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL`.\n- ENDANCHORED post-check (3305-3308