=end_subject` when `oveccount > 0`).\n- Only `subject_length`, `start_offset`, `leftchar`, `rightchar`, `startchar` are filled for `rc >= 0` or PARTIAL. `matchedby = PCRE2_MATCHEDBY_DFA_INTERPRETER`, `mark = NULL` always, `options = original_options`.\n- COPY_MATCHED_SUBJECT handled only for `rc >= 0` (not for partial); prior copied subject freed at 3679-3684.\n- Bumpalong advance is one *character* (UTF-aware), plus CR/LF skip conditioned on `!(re->flags & PCRE2_HASCRORLF)` and newline convention; note DFA does not use the `start_match > subject+start_offset` guard that `pcre2_match` has.\n- On NOMATCH the RWS chain is freed at `EXIT` and `match_data->rc = rc` is set for every path.\n\n# 3. `pcre2_next_match()` — `pcre2_match_next.c:96-169`\n\nSignature `int pcre2_next_match(pcre2_match_data*, PCRE2_SIZE *pstart_offset, uint32_t *poptions)`; returns TRUE/FALSE (an `int` boolean, not a PCRE2 rc). Requires a match_data that has been through `pcre2_match`/`pcre2_dfa_match` (reads `rc`, `start_offset`, `ovector[0..1]`, `subject`, `subject_length`, and `code` → `newline_convention`, `overall_options & PCRE2_UTF`).\n\nExact branch table:\n1. `match_data->rc < 0` (NOMATCH, PARTIAL, or any error) → return FALSE (no retry protocol needed any more).\n2. Asserts `ovector[1] >= start_offset`.\n3. `ovector[0] != start_offset && ovector[1] == start_offset` (the rare `\\K`-in-lookaround case: non-empty-looking match that makes no progress): if `start_offset >= subject_length` → FALSE; else `*pstart_offset = do_bumpalong(md, ovector[1])`, `*poptions = 0`, TRUE.\n4. Empty match `ovector[0] == ovector[1]`: if `ovector[0] >= subject_length` → FALSE; else `*pstart_offset = ovector[1]`, `*poptions = PCRE2_NOTEMPTY_ATSTART`, TRUE (retry at the same point demanding a non-empty match).\n5. Otherwise (normal non-empty match): `*pstart_offset = ovector[1]`, `*poptions = 0`, TRUE.\n\n`do_bumpalong` (49-88): if `subject[offset] == CR && offset+1 < subject_length && subject[offset+1] == LF` and the pattern's newline convention is CRLF/ANY/ANYCRLF → `offset+2`; else in UTF mode advance one whole character (`FORWARDCHARTEST`); else `offset+1`.\n\nNotes for tests: it never inspects `oveccount` beyond pair 0 (so DFA multi-match ovectors are handled by the first/longest pair only); the only options it ever emits are `0` and `PCRE2_NOTEMPTY_ATSTART`; it needs `match_data->subject` non-NULL only on the bumpalong path (case 3). \"dupmatch\"/progress guarantees: callers rely on `start_offset == ovector[1]` except in case 3 — `pcre2_substitute.c:1712-1728` asserts exactly that, and `pcre2_substitute.c:1015-1023` returns `PCRE2_ERROR_INTERNAL_DUPMATCH` if progress (`ovector[1]` strictly advancing, or an empty match immediately after a non-empty one at the same end) is ever violated. There is no ALLUSEDTEXT handling in this file (that is a pcre2test display mode based on `leftchar`/`rightchar`, which `pcre2_next_match` does not read).\n\n# 4. `_pcre2_study()` — `pcre2_study.c:1914-2084`\n\nComputes, in this order, (a) the start-code-unit bitmap or a derived first code unit, (b) `re->minlength`. Returns 0 normally; 1 = SSB_UNKNOWN, 2 = missing capturing bracket, 3 = unlisted opcode (all unreachable/debug).\n\n**Start bits (1930-2043)**\n- Skipped entirely if `re->flags & (PCRE2_FIRSTSET|PCRE2_STARTLINE)` is already set (a known first code unit or a multiline `^` anchor makes it pointless).\n- `set_start_bits()` (1092-1894) returns: `SSB_DONE` (mandatory starters found → results kept), `SSB_CONTINUE`/`SSB_FAIL`/`SSB_TOODEEP` (nothing stored; recursion depth > 1000 → TOODEEP at 1106), `SSB_UNKNOWN` (internal).\n- Branches that produce `SSB_FAIL` (no bitmap at all): the big opcode list at 1136-1208 — `.`/`\\C`/OP_ALLANY, multiline `^`, `$`, `\\b`-less anchors like `\\A`/`\\z`, backreferences (REF/REFI/DNREF/DNREFI), OP_RECURSE, OP_COND/OP_SCOND, all `(*VERB)`s, `(*ACCEPT)`, OP_EXTUNI, and all negated single characters (OP_NOT*); `OP_PROP` unless it is the fake `PT_CLIST