d = SSB_CONTINUE`; `OP_KET*` → immediate `SSB_CONTINUE`. At the outermost level only `SSB_DONE` is usable.\n- Post-processing (1950-2042): the 256-bit map is scanned; if exactly **one** bit is set → convert to `PCRE2_FIRSTSET` with `first_codeunit = a`; if exactly **two** and they are the other case of each other (`fcc` table, or `UCD_OTHERCASE` when utf||ucp, rejecting `UCD_CASESET != 0` multi-case sets) → `PCRE2_FIRSTSET|PCRE2_FIRSTCASELESS`. More than two bits, bit 0xFF/248-0x80 in 16/32-bit mode, or (8-bit UTF) a value > 127 → keep `PCRE2_FIRSTMAPSET` instead. When a first code unit is derived and it equals `re->last_codeunit`, `PCRE2_LASTSET|PCRE2_LASTCASELESS` are cleared and `last_codeunit = 0` (2030-2038) — this is what makes `/a*a/` work.\n\n**Minlength (2053-2081)**\n- Computed only if `!(re->flags & (PCRE2_MATCH_EMPTY|PCRE2_HASACCEPT))` and `re->top_backref <= MAX_CACHE_BACKREF (128)`; otherwise `minlength` stays 0.\n- `find_minlength` (101-767) returns -1 (leave minlength 0) for: `\\C` in UTF mode (388), `(*ACCEPT)`/`OP_ASSERT_ACCEPT` (220-222), or complexity (`*countptr > 1000`, 129). -2/-3 are internal errors.\n- Result clamped: `min > UINT16_MAX → UINT16_MAX`; `branchlength` saturates at UINT16_MAX (141-145) and multiplication overflow is saturated (634).\n- Distinct contributions: literals/`+` repeats add 1; EXACT/TYPEEXACT/CRRANGE add their min count; classes add 1 unless `*`/`?`/`{0,}` (0) or CRRANGE min; `.`/`\\d`/props/`\\X`/`\\R` add 1 (`OP_ANYNL` counts as 1 even though it may match CRLF); assertions, `^ $ \\b \\A \\z`, callouts, verbs, OP_CLOSE, OP_SET_SOM, OP_REVERSE/VREVERSE add 0; `{0}`-quantified groups (BRAZERO/BRAMINZERO/BRAPOSZERO/SKIPZERO) add 0.\n- Groups whose opcode is in `OP_SBRA..OP_SCOND` (\"could be empty\") return 0 immediately (121). A one-branch condition (including DEFINE) adds 0; a two-branch condition is treated as a normal group (150-164).\n- Alternation: minimum over branches, but a branch containing a recursion/backreference-recursion (`had_recurse`) is ignored (236-242); a zero-length branch short-circuits the rest.\n- Backreferences: `PCRE2_MATCH_UNSET_BACKREF` set → 0 (479, 557); `(?|` duplicate numbers used (`PCRE2_DUPCAPUSED`) → 0 for DNREF, and for REF a duplicate-numbered target also yields 0; DNREF takes the minimum over all same-named groups; results cached in `backref_cache` (`recno <= backref_cache[0] && >= 0`); simple or mutual recursion sets `had_recurse`; missing bracket → -2.\n- Repeated backreference multiplies by the quantifier min (0 for `*`/`?`, 1 for `+`, `GET2` for ranges, 1 for none) (599-636).\n- `OP_RECURSE` uses `prev_recurse_recno`/`prev_recurse_d` caching; the special `OP_BRA{OP_RECURSE}OP_KET` wrapper sets `once_fudge` so repeated recursion is measured at the outer level (166-177, 643-675).\n- Capturing groups cache the previous group's length by `recno` unless `PCRE2_DUPCAPUSED` (199-214)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3665,"cache_read_input_tokens":122937,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3665,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01MsTxT1uKmXFxQ5nSxDktsD","session_id":"f125a214-542c-4276-b4c6-bfe5147344e3","uuid":"eb8c76c6-0db5-4521-898b-8f48564e636f","timestamp":"2026-09-04T04:41:12.292Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Analyze match/dfa branching"}
