{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_htuzhm2r7musspqytsy6po6wh5dy6sngzgeng53vkfbshwsntsua","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Files read: `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-Qil4GP/c_src/src/pcre2_substitute.c`, `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-Qil4GP/c_src/src/pcre2_convert.c`, plus the behaviour-defining helpers `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-Qil4GP/c_src/src/pcre2_match_next.c` (`pcre2_next_match`), `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-Qil4GP/c_src/src/pcre2_context.c` (convert-context defaults + setter validation), `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-Qil4GP/c_src/src/pcre2_compile.c` (`PRIV(check_escape)`, `escapes[]` table), `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-Qil4GP/c_src/include/pcre2.h`.\n\n# `pcre2_substitute` (pcre2_substitute.c:742-1793)\n\n## A. Argument-shape configurations (checked before any matching)\n- `*blength` is read as buffer capacity in code units **including** room for the trailing NUL; it is immediately overwritten with `PCRE2_UNSET` (so every error path leaves `PCRE2_UNSET` unless it later sets an offset/length).\n- `mcontext == NULL` vs `!= NULL`. Only a non-NULL mcontext can supply `substitute_callout` and `substitute_case_callout`/`_data`. With NULL mcontext both callouts are absent (default casing path).\n- `replacement == NULL && rlength == 0` → valid, treated as empty string. `replacement == NULL && rlength != 0` → `PCRE2_ERROR_NULL` (invalid).\n- `rlength == PCRE2_ZERO_TERMINATED` (strlen'd) vs explicit length (may contain embedded NULs, which are then literal output bytes).\n- `subject == NULL && length == 0` → valid, empty subject. `subject == NULL && length != 0` → `PCRE2_ERROR_NULL`.\n- `length == PCRE2_ZERO_TERMINATED` vs explicit length (embedded NULs allowed).\n- `start_offset`: `0`, `0 < so < length`, `so == length` (valid; can still match empty/`$`), `so > length` → `PCRE2_ERROR_BADOFFSET` (line 956).\n- `match_data == NULL` → an internal match_data is created from the pattern (memctl from mcontext if non-NULL, else from code). Ovector count = pattern's `top_bracket+1`.\n- `match_data != NULL`, `MATCHED` not set → external block used directly for matching; on return `match_data->rc = rc` is written (only in this configuration).\n- `match_data != NULL`, small ovector (`oveccount < top_bracket+1`) → valid; `rc == 0` from pcre2_match is normalised to `ovector_count` (line 1043); affects `$+` (→ `PCRE2_ERROR_UNAVAILABLE`) and named-group \"first that is set\" scanning (`ng < ovector_count` filter).\n\n## B. `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_MATCHED` configurations\n- Requires `match_data != NULL` (else `PCRE2_ERROR_NULL`, line 827).\n- Valid pre-existing `match_data->rc`: `>= 0` (a match; `0` means ovector was too small) or `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMATCH` (→ 0 substitutions, output = copy of subject). Any other negative rc is returned verbatim.\n- Must not come from the DFA matcher (`matchedby == PCRE2_MATCHEDBY_DFA_INTERPRETER` → `PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_UFUNC`).\n- Must satisfy: `code == match_data->code`; `length == match_data->subject_length` **and** (`subject` pointer identical **or** `PCRE2_MD_COPIED_SUBJECT` set and `memcmp` equal, or `length == 0`); `start_offset == match_data->start_offset`; `options & ~(SUBSTITUTE_OPTIONS|PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK) == match_data->options & ~PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK`. Errors: `DIFFSUBSPATTERN`, `DIFFSUBSSUBJECT`, `DIFFSUBSOFFSET`, `DIFFSUBSOPTIONS`.\n- Two valid sub-cases worth testing separately: subject supplied by pointer identity, and subject supplied via a `PCRE2_COPY_MATCHED_SUBJECT` match_data (content comparison path).\n- When `MATCHED`, an *internal copy* of the match_data is made (`min(top_bracket+1, oveccount)` pairs copied, heapframes cleared, `PCRE2_MD_COPIED_SUBJECT` cleared) — the caller's block is never mutated and its `rc` is **not** updated.\n- `MATCHED` + `GLOBAL`: first substitution uses the supplied match; subsequent ones come from real `pcre2_match` calls.\n- Whenever an internal match_data is in use, `PCRE2_COPY_MATCHED_SUBJECT` is stripped from `options` (line 921).\n\n## C. Option-bit branches (`SUBSTITUTE_OPTIONS` = EXTENDED|GLOBAL|LITERAL|MATCHED|OVERFLOW_LENGTH|REPLACEMENT_ONLY|UNKNOWN_UNSET|UNSET_EMPTY; these are stripped before being passed to `pcre2_match`; all other bits are forwarded to `pcre2_match` unchanged)\n- `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_GLOBAL` clear → exactly one substitution attempt; set → loop driven by `pcre2_next_match`.\n- `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_REPLACEMENT_ONLY` clear → output = pre-`start_offset` text + inter-match text + replacements + post-match tail. Set → output = concatenation of replacements only (no `subject[0..start_offset)`, no leading fragments, no trailing tail).\n- `PCRE2_PARTIAL_HARD` / `PCRE2_PARTIAL_SOFT`: **only valid together with `REPLACEMENT_ONLY`** (otherwise `PCRE2_ERROR_BADOPTION`, line 796, checked before any other validation). Under partial, `$'` and `$_` give `PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIALSUBS`; `` $` `` is still allowed; an actual partial match makes `pcre2_match` return `PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL`, which propagates.\n- `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_LITERAL` → the whole replacement is `memcpy`'d verbatim, once per match; `$`, `\\`, `\\Q`, case forcing and `EXTENDED` are all inert. (LITERAL+EXTENDED is accepted but EXTENDED has no effect — effectively mutually exclusive.)\n- `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_EXTENDED` (only meaningful without LITERAL) enables: backslash escape processing, `\\Q..\\E`, `\\L \\U \\l \\u \\E` case forcing, `\\g<...>`, `\\1`-style backrefs, and the `${n:-...}` / `${n:+...:...}` conditional forms. Without EXTENDED, a `\\` in the replacement is an ordinary literal backslash (so `\\$1` yields backslash followed by group 1 — not an escaped `$`).\n- `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_UNSET_EMPTY` → an unset group in a *plain* (non-`:+`/`:-`) substitution contributes nothing instead of `PCRE2_ERROR_UNSET`. Also applies to `$+` when no group is set. Has no effect inside `${n:+}`/`${n:-}` forms (those handle unset themselves).\n- `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_UNKNOWN_UNSET` → a numeric group `> top_bracket`, an unknown group name, or `$+` with `top_bracket == 0` is treated as \"unset\" instead of `PCRE2_ERROR_NOSUBSTRING`. Combines with UNSET_EMPTY: UNKNOWN_UNSET alone still errors with `PCRE2_ERROR_UNSET`; UNKNOWN_UNSET+UNSET_EMPTY yields empty. Note for numeric groups the remaining digits are skipped (line 1260).\n- `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_OVERFLOW_LENGTH` clear → first overflow immediately returns `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY` with `*blength == PCRE2_UNSET`. Set → scanning continues in \"simulated\" mode accumulating `extra_needed`; returns `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY` with `*blength = buff_length + extra_needed` (total required size **including** the trailing NUL).\n- `PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK`: when the pattern is UTF and this is clear, the *replacement* is UTF-validated (line 938) and the error sets `match_data->startchar`/`leftchar = 0`. It is also forwarded to `pcre2_match`, and after the first match iteration it is forced on internally (line 988) so the subject is only validated once.\n- `PCRE2_NOTEMPTY_ATSTART` may be passed in by the caller (forwarded to `pcre2_match`); it is also what `pcre2_next_match` sets in `goptions` after an empty match. `goptions` is OR'd in only for the internally driven matches.\n\n## D. Buffer-sizing configurations\n- Buffer strictly larger than needed → success, `*blength = buff_offset - 1` (length excluding NUL).\n- Buffer exactly `needed_output + 1` → success (the final `CHECKMEMCPY(temp,1)` at line 1742 writes the NUL; capacity must include it).\n- Buffer exactly `needed_output` (i.e. one short — NUL doesn't fit) → overflow.\n- Buffer `0` and/or `buffer == NULL` with OVERFLOW_LENGTH → pure length query.\n- Overflow can be triggered at each distinct `CHECKMEMCPY` site: pre-start-offset copy, inter-match fragment, whole-literal replacement, group contents, `${*MARK}`, escape-produced char, literal code unit, callout-rejection re-copy of the matched text, trailing tail, trailing NUL. Each is a separate test point.\n- Overflow inside a case-forced region goes through `CHECKCASECPY_*` instead, which computes the *transformed* length; with a case callout and OVERFLOW_LENGTH the estimate uses `pessimistic_case_inflation(n) = n/8 + 10`, so **more than two calls may be needed** to converge on the buffer size.\n- Integer-overflow saturation paths → `PCRE2_ERROR_TOOLARGEREPLACE` (accumulating `extra_needed`, or `buff_length + extra_needed`).\n- `subs == INT_MAX` → `PCRE2_ERROR_TOOMANYREPLACE`.\n\n## E. Replacement-string syntax branches (non-LITERAL scanner, lines 1064-1632)\nNesting/termination:\n- `ptr >= repend` with empty ptr-stack → end of replacement; with non-empty stack → pop and resume the outer text (used by `${n:-}`/`${n:+}` reprocessing).\n- Nesting depth: stack holds 2 entries per level, `PTR_STACK_SIZE == 20` → max 10 nested conditional expansions; deeper → `PCRE2_ERROR_BADREPLACEMENT`.\n- `escaped_literal` (`\\Q` state) is declared at function scope, so it persists across iterations of the global loop — an unterminated `\\Q` in one match keeps literal mode active for the next match.\n\n`$` forms (line 1101):\n- `$` at end of text → BADREPLACEMENT.\n- `$$` → literal `$` (works with or without EXTENDED).\n- `$&` → whole match (group 0).\n- `` $` `` → pre-match text `subject[0, ovector[0])`.\n- `$'` → post-match text `subject[ovector[1], length)`; PARTIALSUBS under partial.\n- `$_` → entire subject; PARTIALSUBS under partial.\n- `$+` → highest-numbered *set* capture group. Sub-branches: `top_bracket == 0` (no groups) → NOSUBSTRING, or UNKNOWN_UNSET→treated as unset; `oveccount < top_bracket+1` → `PCRE2_ERROR_UNAVAILABLE`; all groups unset → UNSET / UNSET_EMPTY. `$+{name}` is *not* `$+` (it falls through to `${`-less name parsing → BADREPLACEMENT), because of the `ptr[1] != '{'` guard.\n- `$<digits>` → numeric group. Multi-digit accepted; `> top_bracket` → NOSUBSTRING or UNKNOWN_UNSET.\n- `$name` (bare, unbraced) → named group; name = `ctype_word` chars (or Unicode L/Nd/`_` in UTF); empty name or `> MAX_NAME_SIZE` → BADREPLACEMENT.\n- `${...}` (`inparens`) → `${digits}`, `${name}`, `${*MARK}`; must be closed by `}` else `PCRE2_ERROR_REPMISSINGBRACE`.\n- `$<name>` (`inangle`) → named groups only; digits and `*` are **not** accepted in this form (`!inangle` guards); missing `>` → BADREPLACEMENT.\n- `$*MARK` / `${*MARK}` (`star`) → the `(*MARK)` name; only the exact string `MARK` is valid (anything else → BADREPLACEMENT); a NULL mark emits nothing; length is taken from `mark[-1]` so embedded NULs are preserved. `*` cannot combine with `$<>` and cannot combine with the `:`-conditional forms.\n- Named-group resolution with duplicate names: picks the first name-table entry whose group is set; else the first entry within the ovector; else `GET2(first)`. Unknown name + UNKNOWN_UNSET → group forced to `top_bracket+1` (always unset).\n\nEXTENDED-only conditional forms (require `inparens && !star && ptr < repend-2 && *ptr == ':'`, line 1290):\n- `${n:-default}` → group set: substitute the group contents; group unset: reprocess `default` as a replacement fragment (recursive, so it may itself contain `$…`, escapes, case forcing).\n- `${n:+ifset}` → group set: reprocess `ifset`; unset: substitute nothing.\n- `${n:+ifset:ifnotset}` → set: reprocess `ifset`; unset: reprocess `ifnotset` (may be empty).\n- `${n:X...}` with `X` neither `+` nor `-` → `PCRE2_ERROR_BADSUBSTITUTION`.\n- Terminator scanning (`find_text_end`, line 76) branches on: unescaped `}` at nest level 0 (end), unescaped `:` at nest level 0 when not the last part, nested `${` increasing nest level, `\\Q…\\E` literal spans (in which `:`/`}` are inert), `\\L \\l \\U \\u` skipped, other escapes validated via `check_escape` (bad escape → `PCRE2_ERROR_BADREPESCAPE`), `\\E` isolated → ignored, `\\g<...>` → skipped leniently, capture-group escapes → skipped. Never finding the terminator → `PCRE2_ERROR_REPMISSINGBRACE`.\n- Same `${n:...}` text with **not**-EXTENDED → the `:` is not `}` so `REPMISSINGBRACE`.\n\nEXTENDED backslash forms (line 1472):\n- Case forcing: `\\U` (upper, until `\\E`), `\\L` (lower, until `\\E`), `\\u` (title-case next char only), `\\l` (lower-case next char only), `\\u\\L` (title first + lower rest — one combined state), `\\l\\U` (lower first + upper rest, \"reverse title\"), `\\E` (cancel). The `\\u\\L`/`\\l\\U` recognition requires `ptr + 2 < repend`, so those digraphs at the very end of the replacement do **not** combine. Setting a new case state flushes any pending delayed transformation.\n- `\\Q` … `\\E` literal span (all characters copied verbatim, `$` inert inside).\n- Data escapes producing a single character: `\\a`(BEL) `\\e`(ESC) `\\f`(FF) `\\n`(LF) `\\r`(CR) `\\t`(HT) `\\b`(backspace 0x08, special-cased at line 1560) `\\v`(vertical tab 0x0b, line 1561); `\\0`, `\\0d`, `\\0dd` and other 1-3 digit octals; `\\o{ddd}`; `\\xhh`; `\\x{h…}`; `\\cX`; and `\\`+non-alphanumeric (e.g. `\\$ \\\\ \\{ \\} \\[ \\] \\( \\) \\^ \\? \\* \\+ \\| \\. \\_ \\` \\: \\; \\< \\= \\> \\@`) which yield the literal character.\n- Back references: `\\1`…`\\9` (and multi-digit when enough captures exist), `\\g{n}`, `\\g<n>` including `\\g<0>`; produce `group = -rc - 1` and take the GROUP_SUBSTITUTE path (so UNSET_EMPTY / UNKNOWN_UNSET apply).\n- `\\g<name>` → named group substitute; requires literal `<`, a valid name, and `>` — otherwise `PCRE2_ERROR_BADREPESCAPE`.\n- Rejected with `PCRE2_ERROR_BADREPESCAPE`: `\\` at end of text; every \"special\" escape (`\\A \\B \\C \\D \\G \\H \\K \\N \\P \\R \\S \\W \\X \\Z \\d \\h \\k \\p \\s \\w \\z`); and, because `check_escape` is called with `cb == NULL`, anything else non-table (`\\F \\i \\j \\m \\q \\y \\O \\T \\Y \\u`/`\\U` in check_escape, etc. → ERR3). Also malformed `\\x{`, `\\o{`, out-of-range/surrogate values.\n- Non-EXTENDED: a `\\` is just a literal backslash code unit.\n- Plain literal code unit: read with `GETCHARINCTEST` so a whole UTF character (1-4 units) is copied as one item; this matters for `\\u`/`\\l` single-character casing.\n\nCase-forcing execution modes (two distinct code paths that must both be tested):\n- `substitute_case_callout == NULL` → `default_substitute_case_callout` applied immediately per copied item, source and destination disjoint. Branches inside it: `input_len == 0` early return; `to_case` = LOWER / UPPER / TITLE_FIRST (mutates state to LOWER after first char) / REVERSE_TITLE_FIRST (mutates to UPPER); `single_char` TRUE (transform first char, `memcpy` the rest, state → NONE) vs FALSE; UTF/UCP + `ch >= 128` → `UCD_OTHERCASE`, else the 8-bit `cbit_upper`/`cbit_lower`/`fcc` tables; output overflow (keeps counting the required length); `~(PCRE2_SIZE)0` on length integer overflow.\n- `substitute_case_callout != NULL` → transformation is **deferred**: characters accumulate untransformed and `DELAYEDFORCECASE()` runs in-place over `[casestart_offset, buff_offset)` at each case-state change and at the end of the replacement. Valid `to_case` values passed to the *user* callout are only `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_CASE_LOWER` (1), `UPPER` (2), `TITLE_FIRST` (3) — internal state 4 (`REVERSE_TITLE_FIRST`) is decomposed into LOWER(first char)+UPPER(rest), and `\\u`/`\\l` single-char modes are decomposed into TITLE_FIRST/LOWER(first char) + verbatim rest.\n- Callout return-value branches in `do_case_copy`: `rc <= ch1_cap` (fits in the vacated space), `ch1_cap < rc <= max_ch1_cap` (loop again after `memmove`-ing the tail right — the loop tolerates a callout that returns different lengths for identical input), `rc > max_ch1_cap` (`ch1_overflow`, second half called with a dummy 0-capacity buffer), and `rc == ~(PCRE2_SIZE)0` → `PCRE2_ERROR_REPLACECASE`.\n- `forcecase` is reset to `{NONE, FALSE}` at the top of every global-loop iteration, i.e. case forcing never leaks from one match to the next (unlike `escaped_literal`).\n\n## F. Substitute callout branches (lines 1648-1710)\n- Called only when `mcontext != NULL && mcontext->substitute_callout != NULL` **and** `overflowed == FALSE`.\n- Block contents: `version = 0`, `input = subject`, `output = buffer`, `ovector`, `oveccount = rc` (post-normalisation), `subscount = subs` (1-based, counted before the callout), `output_offsets[0]` = start of this replacement, `output_offsets[1]` = end.\n- Return `0` → accept the replacement; substitution counted.\n- Return `> 0` → reject *this* substitution: `buff_offset`/`lengthleft` rewound by the replacement length and the original matched text `subject[ovector[0], ovector[1])` copied instead — **but only if `!REPLACEMENT_ONLY`**; with REPLACEMENT_ONLY the matched text is dropped entirely. The substitution still counts toward the returned `subs` and toward `subscount`. Global loop continues.\n- Return `< 0` → same rejection behaviour, plus `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_GLOBAL` is cleared so the loop ends after this match.\n- `overflowed == TRUE` → the callout is **not** called and cannot be; the sizing is pessimistic: `extra_needed += max(0, oldlength - newlength)` so the reported length covers both accept and reject outcomes. Test: OVERFLOW_LENGTH + rejecting callout, then a second call with the reported size must succeed.\n\n## G. Empty-match / global-advance logic (line 1715 + `pcre2_next_match`)\n- Not GLOBAL, or `pcre2_next_match` returns FALSE → `start_offset = ovector[1]`, exit loop.\n- Non-empty match → next attempt at `ovector[1]` with `goptions = 0`.\n- Empty match at `ovector[0] == ovector[1] >= subject_length` → stop.\n- Empty match not at end → retry at the **same** offset with `PCRE2_NOTEMPTY_ATSTART`; if that yields a non-empty match at the same point it is substituted; if NOMATCH the loop ends. There is no bumpalong copy in substitute (line 1728 asserts `start_offset == ovector[1]`).\n- `\\K` cases: `ovector[1] < ovector[0]` or `ovector[0] < start_offset` → `PCRE2_ERROR_BADSUBSPATTERN` (line 1001), so the `ovector[0] != start_offset && ovector[1] == start_offset` bumpalong branch in `pcre2_next_match` is unreachable from substitute.\n- The progress assertion (line 1015) accepts only: `ovector[1]` strictly advanced, or an empty match at the same end position immediately after a non-empty match; otherwise `PCRE2_ERROR_INTERNAL_DUPMATCH`.\n- `pcre2_next_match` also handles CRLF/UTF-aware bumpalong for `PCRE2_NEWLINE_CRLF/ANY/ANYCRLF` — reachable only via the `\\K` branch, so not from substitute.\n\n## H. Return/output contract\n- Success: return value = number of substitutions (0 allowed), `*blength` = output length excluding the NUL, buffer NUL-terminated.\n- `NOROOM` → `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY`, `*blength` left `PCRE2_UNSET`.\n- Overflow-length mode → `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY`, `*blength` = required total.\n- Replacement-syntax errors (`BADREPLACEMENT`, `BADREPESCAPE`, `BADSUBSTITUTION`, `REPMISSINGBRACE`, `UNSET`, `NOSUBSTRING`, `UNAVAILABLE`, `PARTIALSUBS`) set `*blength` to the **offset in the replacement string** (`ptr - replacement`) — including inside reprocessed `${…}` fragments, where the offset is relative to the original `replacement` pointer.\n- `PCRE2_ERROR_REPLACECASE`, `TOOLARGEREPLACE`, `TOOMANYREPLACE`, `BADSUBSPATTERN`, `BADOFFSET`, `NOMEMORY`(alloc) leave `*blength == PCRE2_UNSET`.\n\n## I. Mutually exclusive / invalid combinations (substitute)\n- PARTIAL_HARD|PARTIAL_SOFT without REPLACEMENT_ONLY → BADOPTION (rejected before anything else).\n- MATCHED without match_data → NULL.\n- MATCHED with a DFA-produced match_data → DFA_UFUNC.\n- MATCHED with mismatched code/subject/length/start_offset/non-substitute options → the four `DIFFSUBS*` errors.\n- LITERAL makes EXTENDED, `$`-processing, `\\`-processing, `\\Q`, and case forcing all inert (accepted, but nothing to test beyond a verbatim copy).\n- `${n:+…}` / `${n:-…}` require EXTENDED **and** braces **and** no `*`.\n- `$<…>` excludes both digits and `*`.\n- `$+{` is never `$+`.\n- `\\u\\L` / `\\l\\U` combining requires at least 3 code units of remaining text.\n- The user case callout never receives `to_case == 0` or `4`.\n- `substitute_case_callout` requires a non-NULL `mcontext`; the default (immediate) casing path requires disjoint source/destination and is therefore only used for subject/mark/`temp` sources.\n\n# `pcre2_pattern_convert` (pcre2_convert.c:1116-1237)\n\n## A. Argument / option validation\n- `pattern == NULL && plength == 0` → valid, empty pattern.\n- `pattern == NULL && plength != 0`, or `bufflenptr == NULL` → `PCRE2_ERROR_NULL` (`*bufflenptr = 0` if it exists).\n- `plength == PCRE2_ZERO_TERMINATED` vs explicit length.\n- `options & ~ALL_OPTIONS` (undefined bit) → BADOPTION; more than one type bit → BADOPTION; no type bit → BADOPTION. So exactly one of `PCRE2_CONVERT_GLOB`, `PCRE2_CONVERT_POSIX_BASIC`, `PCRE2_CONVERT_POSIX_EXTENDED`.\n- `ALL_OPTIONS` also permits `PCRE2_CONVERT_UTF`, `PCRE2_CONVERT_NO_UTF_CHECK`, `PCRE2_CONVERT_GLOB_NO_WILD_SEPARATOR`, `PCRE2_CONVERT_GLOB_NO_STARSTAR`. The two GLOB_* bits are *accepted but ignored* when the type is POSIX (`convert_posix` never looks at options besides the type).\n- `ccontext == NULL` → `PRIV(default_convert_context)`: separator `/` and escape `\\` on non-Windows, separator `\\` and escape `` ` `` under `_WIN32`.\n- `PCRE2_CONVERT_UTF` without Unicode support → `PCRE2_ERROR_UNICODE_NOT_SUPPORTED`. With Unicode and without `NO_UTF_CHECK`: pattern is UTF-validated; failure sets `*bufflenptr = erroroffset` and returns the UTF error. With `NO_UTF_CHECK` the check is skipped (`NO_UTF_CHECK` alone, without UTF, is inert).\n- `PCRE2_CONVERT_GLOB` passes `options & ~PCRE2_CONVERT_GLOB` down; `convert_posix` receives `pattype` only.\n\n## B. Output-buffer configurations (the three distinct modes)\n1. `buffptr == NULL` → **length-only query**: `dummyrun = TRUE`, converter writes into the 100-unit `dummy_buffer`, one pass, returns 0 with `*bufflenptr` = required length excluding the trailing NUL. `bufflenptr` input value is ignored.\n2. `buffptr != NULL && *buffptr == NULL` → **two passes**: pass 1 is a dummy run to size, then `PRIV(memctl_malloc)(sizeof(pcre2_memctl) + (*bufflenptr+1)*width)` (freed later by `pcre2_converted_pattern_free`), then pass 2 runs for real with `use_length = *bufflenptr + 1`. Allocation failure → `NOMEMORY` with `*bufflenptr = 0`.\n3. `buffptr != NULL && *buffptr != NULL` → **caller-supplied buffer**: `use_buffer = *buffptr`, `use_length = *bufflenptr` (so the caller's length must include room for the NUL), single pass, too-small → `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY`. Sub-cases to test: exact fit (`needed+1`), one short, zero length.\n- Note the asymmetry: `convert_glob` counts length with `output_size` and truncates writes (never overflows the dummy buffer, and reports NOMEMORY only via the final `output_size != written` check), whereas `convert_posix` returns `NOMEMORY` from `PUTCHARS`/bounds checks as soon as a single item doesn't fit (it resets `p` to the buffer start each iteration during a dummy run, so the 100-unit dummy is always adequate in practice).\n- On any converter error, `*bufflenptr` is an **offset into the input pattern** (`pattern - pattern_start` for glob; `convlength`/`plength` semantics for posix — pre-initialised to `plength`); on success it is the output length excluding NUL.\n\n## C. `convert_posix` (BASIC and EXTENDED) input shapes\n- Output always begins with `(*NUL)`.\n- `extended = (pattype & PCRE2_CONVERT_POSIX_EXTENDED)`; every branch below differs between BRE and ERE.\n- State machine: `POSIX_START_REGEX` → `POSIX_ANCHORED` (after a BRE leading `^`) → `POSIX_NOT_BRACKET`, plus in-class states `CLASS_NOT_STARTED` / `CLASS_STARTING` / `CLASS_STARTED`.\n- Inside a bracket expression:\n  - `]` closes it (state → NOT_BRACKET).\n  - `[` inside a class → `CLASS_STARTING`; then `:` → `CLASS_STARTED`; then a run of lowercase letters stays STARTED; then `:` followed by `]` emits `:]` and consumes both (i.e. `[[:alpha:]]`, `[[:digit:][:space:]]`).\n  - A `:` in STARTED state *not* followed by `]` drops back to `CLASS_NOT_STARTED` and the char is copied.\n  - A literal `\\` inside a class is doubled to `\\\\` (POSIX classes have no escapes).\n  - Any other char is copied verbatim (`clength` units, UTF-safe).\n  - Unterminated class at end of pattern → `PCRE2_ERROR_MISSING_SQUARE_BRACKET`.\n- Class opening `[`: leading `^` and then leading `]` are copied through as-is (so `[]]`, `[^]]`, `[^abc]`, `[]abc]` all round-trip).\n- `\\` outside a class:\n  - at end of pattern → `PCRE2_ERROR_END_BACKSLASH`.\n  - ERE → next char is a literal (escaped if it is one of `\\?*+|.^${}[]()`).\n  - BRE → if the next char is in `(){}123456789`: for digits emit `\\` then the digit (back-reference `\\1`…`\\9`); for `( ) { }` emit the bare metacharacter (so `\\(`→`(`, `\\)`→`)`, `\\{`→`{`, `\\}`→`}`), and `lastspecial` records it. Any other char → treated as a literal.\n- `(` → `bracount++`; ERE emits `(`, BRE escapes it to `\\(`.\n- `)` → ERE with `bracount > 0`: `bracount--`, emit `)`; ERE with `bracount == 0` **or** BRE: escaped literal `\\)`.\n- `? + { } |` → ERE: emitted as-is (metacharacters); BRE: escaped literals.\n- `.` and `$` → always emitted as-is in both dialects, state → NOT_BRACKET.\n- `*`:\n  - immediately after another `*` (`lastspecial == '*'`) → dropped (collapses `**`, `***`).\n  - BRE at start of regex / after `^` (`posix_state < POSIX_NOT_BRACKET`) or right after `\\(` → escaped literal `\\*`.\n  - otherwise emitted as `*`.\n- `^`:\n  - ERE → always emitted as `^` (anchor anywhere).\n  - BRE at `POSIX_START_REGEX` or right after `\\(` → emitted as `^`, state → `POSIX_ANCHORED`.\n  - BRE elsewhere → falls through to the default branch → escaped literal `\\^`.\n- Default: any character in `\\?*+|.^${}[]()` (and `c < 255`) is prefixed with `\\`; the character is then copied (`clength` units, so UTF multi-unit characters work); `lastspecial = 0xff`; state → NOT_BRACKET. This is also the path taken for `nextisliteral` characters (`sc` forced to 0).\n- Worth-testing shapes: `a*`, `*a` (BRE literal star), `^*`, `\\(a\\)\\1` (BRE group + backref), `(a|b)+` (ERE), `a\\{2,3\\}` (BRE interval) vs `a{2,3}` (ERE), `[[:alpha:]-z]`, `[]-]`, `[^]a]`, trailing `\\`, unterminated `[`, `$` mid-pattern, UTF multi-byte literals.\n\n## D. `convert_glob` input shapes\nSeparator / escape configuration:\n- `separator` = `ccontext->glob_separator`, settable only to `/`, `\\`, or `.` (`pcre2_set_glob_separator`, otherwise `PCRE2_ERROR_BADDATA`). Default `/` (POSIX) or `\\` (Windows).\n- `escape` = `ccontext->glob_escape`, settable to `0` (**no escape character at all** — every `escape != 0 &&` guard turns off) or any ASCII punctuation from `globpunct`. Default `\\` (POSIX) or `` ` `` (Windows).\n- `with_escape` = separator is one of `\\?*+|.^${}[]()` → the separator is emitted as `\\`+sep. TRUE for separator `\\` and `.`; FALSE for `/`. This changes every generated `[^sep]`, `(?<!sep)`, and `(?:.*?sep)??` fragment.\n- `PCRE2_CONVERT_UTF` with `separator >= 128 || escape >= 128` → `PCRE2_ERROR_CONVERT_SYNTAX` with `*bufflenptr = 0` (unreachable through the public setters).\nPrologue:\n- Output always begins with `(?s)`.\n- `\\A` is emitted **unless** the pattern begins with `*` and either `NO_WILD_SEPARATOR` is set, or (`!NO_STARSTAR` and the pattern begins with `**`).\nPer-character branches:\n- `*` with `NO_STARSTAR` set, or a single `*`:\n  - runs of `*` are collapsed.\n  - `NO_WILD_SEPARATOR` + `*` at end of pattern → `no_slash_z = TRUE` (no trailing `\\z`), loop ends.\n  - `NO_WILD_SEPARATOR` + leading `*` → nothing emitted at all.\n  - not at start: emit `(?>` (opening an atomic group closed at the next `*`/end, `in_atomic`) if a `**` was seen earlier, else emit `(*COMMIT)`.\n  - then emit `.` (NO_WILD_SEPARATOR) or `[^sep]`, followed by `*?`, or `*+` if the `*` was the last thing in the pattern.\n- `**` (only when `!NO_STARSTAR`), sub-branches:\n  - `after_separator` = at start of pattern, or the character before the first `*` is the separator.\n  - `**` (possibly `***…`) at end of pattern → `no_slash_z = TRUE`, loop ends (matches everything to the end).\n  - sets `after_starstar` (which changes later `*` handling to atomic groups).\n  - if `after_separator` and the next chars are `escape` + `separator`, the escape char is skipped.\n  - leading `**` not followed by the separator → emits nothing (continue).\n  - leading `**/` → emits `(?:\\A|` sep `)` and consumes the separator (so `**/foo` matches `foo` and `a/foo`).\n  - non-leading `**` not followed by the separator (or not after a separator) → `(*COMMIT)` + `.*?`.\n  - non-leading `/**/` → `(*COMMIT)` + `(?:.*?` sep `)??` and consumes the separator (so `a/**/b` matches `a/b`).\n- `?` → `.` (NO_WILD_SEPARATOR) or `[^sep]`.\n- `[` → `convert_glob_parse_range` (below).\n- escape character (when `escape != 0`) → the following character is literal; escape as the final character → `PCRE2_ERROR_CONVERT_SYNTAX`.\n- any other char → prefixed with `\\` if it is in `\\?*+|.^${}[]()` and `< 255`, then written.\nEpilogue:\n- `\\z` appended unless `no_slash_z`; `)` appended if an atomic group is still open; trailing NUL written; and in a non-dummy run `output_size != (output - use_buffer)` → `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY`.\nBracket-expression shapes (`convert_glob_parse_range`, line 636):\n- `[` at end of pattern → `MISSING_SQUARE_BRACKET`.\n- Negation via `[!…]` **or** `[^…]` → output starts `[^`, and unless `NO_WILD_SEPARATOR` the separator is added to the negated set (with `\\` if `with_escape`); `!`/`^` as the last char → `MISSING_SQUARE_BRACKET`.\n- Non-negated → output starts `[`.\n- Leading `]` (i.e. `[]…]`, `[!]…]`) → emitted as `\\]`, counts as a member and sets `prev_c` for a following range.\n- Closing `]`: for a *non-negated* class, if `!NO_WILD_SEPARATOR` and the separator is a member (`separator_seen`), a `(?<!sep)` lookbehind is appended after the class.\n- `[:name:]` POSIX class inside the glob class: recognised names are exactly `alpha lower upper alnum ascii blank cntrl digit graph print punct space word xdigit` (indices 1-14); a malformed `[:` (no closing `:]`, or an unknown name) makes the `[` an ordinary member. When recognised and the class is not negated, membership of the separator is tested with `convert_glob_char_in_class` using **`PRIV(default_tables)`** (not the ccontext tables), and `c > 0xff` in 16/32-bit modes always reports \"not a member\". Class-specific quirks: `alpha` excludes `_` and digits; `alnum` excludes `_`; `ascii` = cntrl ∪ print; `blank` = space minus LF/VT/FF/CR.\n- Range `a-z`: requires a preceding member and the next char not being `]`. Range end may itself be escaped. `[:` as the range end → `PCRE2_ERROR_CONVERT_SYNTAX`. `prev_c > c` (reversed range) → `PCRE2_ERROR_CONVERT_SYNTAX`. If `prev_c < separator < c` → `separator_seen`. `prev_c` is reset afterwards, so `a-c-e` treats the second `-` as a literal.\n- `-` as the last member before `]`, or with no preceding member → literal, emitted as `\\-`.\n- Escaped member (`escape` char inside the class) → next char literal; escape as the last char → falls out of the loop → `MISSING_SQUARE_BRACKET`.\n- Members `[`, `]`, `\\`, `-` are always emitted `\\`-prefixed.\n- A member equal to the separator sets `separator_seen`.\n- Reaching the end of the pattern without `]` → `MISSING_SQUARE_BRACKET`.\n- UTF: members and range endpoints are read with `GETCHARINCTEST`, so multi-code-unit characters are valid members/endpoints.\n\n## E. Mutually exclusive / invalid combinations (convert)\n- Exactly one type bit; zero or two+ → BADOPTION.\n- `GLOB_NO_WILD_SEPARATOR` / `GLOB_NO_STARSTAR` are inert with the POSIX types.\n- `NO_UTF_CHECK` is inert without `CONVERT_UTF`.\n- `NO_WILD_SEPARATOR` + `NO_STARSTAR`: NO_WILD_SEPARATOR is tested first in the leading-`*` `\\A` decision and inside `*` handling, so the starstar path is unreachable for the `\\A` choice; `NO_STARSTAR` alone still permits `**` to be treated as a collapsed single `*`.\n- `escape == 0