{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_x7emtnnuatgvv6ugh4vefgbkrxi5wbs7u2wilusc6gcelrgi2pza","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done.\n\n## Deliverable\n\n`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-Qil4GP/translation/ERRORS.md` — **410 numbered rows**, contiguous 1…410, valid GitHub markdown (verified: 0 malformed table lines; all embedded `|` characters escaped). `grep -c '^| [0-9]' translation/ERRORS.md` → **410**.\n\nColumns are exactly `# | function | trigger | expected C result`, grouped into 14 `##` sections (compile-args, compile-patterns ERR1–ERR120, match, dfa_match, substitute, substring, serialize, context/set_*, config, pattern_info/callout_enumerate, convert, match_data/code_copy/maketables/jit/next_match/get_error_message, valid_utf, generic FFI boundary).\n\n## Method actually used\n\nBeyond grepping the C sources, I drove the built `c_src/build/libpcre2.so` directly via Python `ctypes` and **executed every concrete trigger**, recording the real return value. The table is empirically verified, not inferred.\n\n## Key findings the caller should know\n\n1. **The build config is not what `c_src/src/config.h` says.** `config.h` has `SUPPORT_UNICODE` and `SUPPORT_JIT` both `#undef`'d, but `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` adds `-DSUPPORT_UNICODE` (and `PCRE2_CODE_UNIT_WIDTH=8`, `HAVE_CONFIG_H`). Confirmed at runtime: `pcre2_config_8(PCRE2_CONFIG_UNICODE)` → 1, `(PCRE2_CONFIG_JIT)` → 0.\n   - Consequence: **`ERR32`, `ERR45`, `ERR96` are unreachable** (Unicode *is* present), as are `ERR85` and `ERR91` (16-bit only).\n   - **All `pcre2_jit_*` entry points are hard-fail stubs**: `pcre2_jit_compile_8` → `PCRE2_ERROR_JIT_BADOPTION (-45)`, `pcre2_jit_match_8` → `-45`, `pcre2_jit_stack_create_8` → `NULL`, and `PCRE2_JIT_TEST_ALLOC` alone → `PCRE2_ERROR_JIT_UNSUPPORTED (-68)`.\n\n2. **`ERR59` is a retired slot** — the message string is \"obsolete error (should not occur)\" and `ERR59` is never assigned anywhere in `c_src`. A Rust port must keep the numbering hole.\n\n3. **Three real crash-on-NULL sites found in the C code** (not error returns — these are UB, and a Rust port that returns an error instead will *differ*):\n   - `pcre2_substitute_8` reads `code->overall_options` (`pcre2_substitute.c:758`) and `*blength` (`:777`) before any NULL check. **Verified: passing `outlengthptr = NULL` segfaults the C library.**\n   - `pcre2_general_context_copy_8` (and the other three `*_context_copy_8`) dereference `ctx->memctl.malloc` with no NULL check.\n   - `pcre2_get_mark_8` / `get_ovector_*` / `get_startchar_8` / `get_match_data_size_8` / `pcre2_next_match_8` / `pcre2_get_error_message_8` have no NULL guards and no error channel.\n\n4. **Two \"clamp, don't reject\" behaviours** that are easy to get wrong: `pcre2_match_data_create_8(0, …)` clamps *up* to 1 and `(0xffffffff, …)` clamps *down* to `UINT16_MAX` (65535) — neither fails.\n\n5. **`pcre2_pattern_info_8` writes the value even when it returns an error**: `PCRE2_INFO_DEPTHLIMIT`/`HEAPLIMIT`/`MATCHLIMIT` store `UINT32_MAX` into `*where` and *then* return `PCRE2_ERROR_UNSET (-55)`. Also, `code == NULL` with `where == NULL` returns the field size (4), because the NULL-code check happens after the length branch.\n\n6. **`pcre2_pattern_convert_8` mixes positive and negative codes**: `PCRE2_ERROR_MISSING_SQUARE_BRACKET (=106)` and `PCRE2_ERROR_END_BACKSLASH (=101)` are returned as *positive* compile-error numbers alongside negative `-64`/`-48`/`-51`.\n\n7. Triggers I could not drive from outside (flagged in-table rather than omitted): `ERR10, 20*, 23, 31, 52, 53, 56, 63, 70, 72, 80, 86, 89, 90`, `PCRE2_ERROR_BAD_BACKSLASH_K (-75)`, `TOOLARGEREPLACE (-70)`, `TOOMANYREPLACE (-61)`, `INTERNAL_DUPMATCH (-65)`, `INVALIDOFFSET (-67)`. (*`ERR20` *is* reachable — `(?:(?:(?:(?:a{255}){255}){255}){255})`.) `-75` in particular is compile-blocked as `ERR99` for all direct spellings; I brute-forced 12 recursion-based `\\K` patterns × 7 subjects × all offsets without hitting it.\n\n## One cleanup item for you\n\n`rm` is blocked by my sandbox, so my verification scratch directory is still on disk: **`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-Qil4GP/_verify/`** (Python ctypes harnesses `h.py`, `r.py`, `t1–t5.py`, `rt1–rt16.py`, `final.py`, plus `__pycache__`). Delete it, or keep it — the scripts are a ready-made differential-test oracle against the C library. `c_src/` was not modified and no Rust or tests were written."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2803,"cache_read_input_tokens":263138,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2803,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01UKchETTuuMqzXECbY47gbA","session_id":"f125a214-542c-4276-b4c6-bfe5147344e3","uuid":"2eeb1281-cadf-403d-8113-e6fcf89d6421","timestamp":"2026-09-04T04:56:52.827Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Build ERRORS.md error surface"}
