{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_fgspsnucls3fexrvtrmqgylnqo2ticaprpfl2snqejvpireimfmq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01BsTNAemmrnQ1j1CTXzp7cG","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Phase C match/dfa/utf error tests","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"Working dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-Qil4GP\nCrate: `translation/` — run ALL cargo commands from there and ALWAYS pass `--offline`\n(the crates.io network is blocked; `libloading` is already vendored in the local cache).\n\nTASK: write ONE new file `translation/tests/match_errors.rs` with differential\nerror-path tests (C `.so` vs Rust `.so`, both via libloading) covering EXACTLY these\nsections of `translation/ERRORS.md`:\n  * **section C** — `pcre2_match_8` (rows 173–198)\n  * **section D** — `pcre2_dfa_match_8` (rows 199–226)\n  * **section M** — `_pcre2_valid_utf_8` and the UTF errors it surfaces (rows 458–479)\nRead those sections of `translation/ERRORS.md` FIRST — it is the spec. Every row in\nthose three sections must end up with a passing test.\n\nDo NOT touch any other file in `translation/tests/` (other agents are working there).\nDo NOT modify `c_src/`. If you find a genuine divergence, fix the RUST source under\n`translation/src/`, never the C and never the test's expectations.\n\n## Existing harness — USE IT, do not rewrite it\n`translation/tests/common/mod.rs` gives `pub fn both() -> (&'static Api, &'static Api)`\nreturning (C, Rust). `Api` holds raw `extern \"C\"` fn pointers, including:\n  compile, code_free, match_data_create, match_data_create_from_pattern, match_data_free,\n  do_match (= `pcre2_match_8`), dfa_match, jit_match, jit_compile,\n  get_ovector_pointer, get_ovector_count, get_mark, get_startchar, next_match,\n  match_context_create, match_context_free, set_match_limit, set_depth_limit,\n  set_heap_limit, set_offset_limit, set_callout, set_recursion_memory_management,\n  valid_utf (= `_pcre2_valid_utf_8`), get_error_message, pattern_info,\n  general_context_create, general_context_free, compile_context_create, ...\n`Api.name` is \"C\" or \"Rust\". `pub struct Rng` is a seeded xorshift PRNG:\n`new(seed)`, `next_u32`, `below(n)`, `range(lo,hi)`, `pick(&[T])`, `bool()`,\n`bytes_from(len,&alphabet)`, `raw_bytes(len)`.\n\n`translation/tests/common/diff.rs` (module `common::diff`) has:\n  * every `PCRE2_*` constant, already verified against `c_src/include/pcre2.h`\n    (options, `PCRE2_ZERO_TERMINATED`, `PCRE2_UNSET`, `ERR_NOMATCH`, `ERR_PARTIAL`,\n    `ERR_NULL`, `ERR_BADDATA`, `ERR_BADMAGIC`, `ERR_BADOPTION`, `ERR_BADOFFSET`,\n    `ERR_NOMEMORY`, `ERR_UNSET`, `ERR_BADOFFSETLIMIT`, `ERR_JIT_BADOPTION`, …)\n  * `CompileCfg::new(opts)` with `.extra()`, `.newline()`, `.bsr()`, `.own_tables()`,\n    `.max_len()`, `.parens_nest()`, `.optimize()`, …\n  * `compile_in(api, pat, patlen, &cfg) -> Compiled` (`.code`, `.errorcode`,\n    `.erroroffset`; auto-frees on drop)\n  * `compile_both(pat, patlen, &cfg, label) -> (Compiled, Compiled)` — already asserts\n    equal errorcode / erroroffset / all `pattern_info` / serialized bytecode\n  * `MatchCfg::new(opts)` with `.ovec(n)`, `.match_limit(n)`, `.depth_limit(n)`,\n    `.heap_limit(n)`, `.offset_limit(n)`\n  * `Engine::{Interpreter, Dfa, JitMatch}`, `run_match(api, code, subj, subjlen,\n    startoffset, &mcfg, engine) -> MatchOut`, `assert_match_eq(...)`,\n    `assert_pattern_info_eq(cc, rc, label)`, `serialized_bytes(api, code)`\nStart the file with:\n```rust\nmod common;\nuse common::diff::*;\nuse common::*;\n```\nStudy `translation/tests/api_errors.rs` and `translation/tests/compile_errors.rs` for\nthe established style (one `#[test]` per row-group, named `rowNNN_...`, rich assert\nmessages, and a dedicated test that DOCUMENTS rows which are undefined behaviour).\n\n## Specific things to get right\n1. **Never compare undefined memory.** After a match, only ovector pairs `0..rc` are\n   defined; `rc == 0` means \"ovector too small, all pairs filled\"; on\n   `PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL` only pair 0 is set; on any other negative rc NOTHING is\n   defined. `run_match` in the harness already implements this rule — prefer it over\n   reading the ovector yourself.\n2. `pcre2_match_data_create_8` CLAMPS rather than fails: `0` becomes 1 and\n   `0xffffffff` becomes 65535. Assert the clamping agrees (via `get_ovector_count`).\n3. `pcre2_pattern_info_8` writes `UINT32_MAX` and THEN returns `PCRE2_ERROR_UNSET`.\n4. Cover these match-side rejections at minimum (check ERRORS.md for the exact set):\n   `startoffset > length` -> `PCRE2_ERROR_BADOFFSET`; a `startoffset` landing\n   mid-UTF-8-character -> `PCRE2_ERROR_BADUTFOFFSET`; invalid UTF-8 subject ->\n   the specific negative `PCRE2_ERROR_UTF8_ERRn`; undefined match-option bits ->\n   `PCRE2_ERROR_BADOPTION`; `PCRE2_PARTIAL_HARD|PCRE2_PARTIAL_SOFT` together;\n   `DFA_RESTART`/`DFA_SHORTEST` passed to `pcre2_match_8` (interpreter) ->\n   `PCRE2_ERROR_BADOPTION`; offset_limit set without `PCRE2_USE_OFFSET_LIMIT` ->\n   `PCRE2_ERROR_BADOFFSETLIMIT`; match/depth/heap limit exceeded ->\n   `PCRE2_ERROR_MATCHLIMIT` / `DEPTHLIMIT` / `HEAPLIMIT`; `code == NULL`;\n   `code` pointing at junk -> `PCRE2_ERROR_BADMAGIC`; `match_data == NULL`;\n   `pcre2_jit_match_8` in this non-JIT build -> `PCRE2_ERROR_JIT_BADOPTION (-45)`;\n   `pcre2_jit_compile_8` -> `PCRE2_ERROR_JIT_UNSUPPORTED`-family result.\n   For dfa_match additionally: `wscount` too small -> `PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_WSSIZE`,\n   `PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_UITEM` for items the DFA cannot handle (`\\C` in UTF mode,\n   backreferences, `(?=...)` recursion — grep pcre2_dfa_match.c for `DFA_UITEM`,\n   `DFA_UCOND`, `DFA_UINVALID_UTF`, `DFA_BADRESTART`), and `PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_RECURSE`.\n5. **Exhaustive option-bit sweeps** are cheap and valuable: for every one of the 32\n   bits of the match `options` word, call both libraries and assert identical rc, for\n   `pcre2_match_8` AND `pcre2_dfa_match_8`.\n6. For section M, sweep `_pcre2_valid_utf_8` directly: all 256 single bytes, all 65536\n   two-byte sequences, randomized 3–6 byte sequences (fixed seed, >= 50 000 cases),\n   and assert BOTH the return code AND the `*erroroffset` agree. Then assert the SAME\n   UTF error codes surface through `pcre2_compile_8` (with `PCRE2_UTF`),\n   `pcre2_match_8` and `pcre2_dfa_match_8` on invalid subjects.\n7. **KNOWN UB — do NOT call these**, just document them in a test with a comment\n   (calling them crashes the C library too, so there is no correct answer to compare):\n   * `PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK` together with genuinely invalid UTF-8 (documented UB;\n     verified to segfault BOTH libraries).\n   * `PCRE2_DFA_RESTART` with a workspace that did NOT come from a previous PARTIAL\n     match (verified to segfault BOTH libraries).\n   * `pcre2_get_mark_8` / `get_ovector_*` / `get_startchar_8` / `next_match_8` with a\n     NULL match_data (no NULL guard in the C).\n   For DFA_RESTART, test the DOCUMENTED flow instead: a `PCRE2_PARTIAL_HARD` dfa_match\n   first, then re-call with `PCRE2_DFA_RESTART` and the SAME workspace, comparing the\n   workspace contents and the final result between the libraries.\n8. Some deeply-recursive patterns need a big stack; the suite is run with\n   `RUST_MIN_STACK=67108864`. Avoid patterns that recurse without bound.\n\n## Build / iterate\n```\ncd translation\ncargo build --offline --release          # produces the Rust .so the tests load\nRUST_MIN_STACK=67108864 cargo test --offline --test match_errors -- --test-threads=1\n```\n(The C `.so` is already built at `c_src/build/libpcre2.so`. If you need to rebuild it:\n`cd c_src/build && cmake --build .`)\n\n## Deliverable / self-verification before you finish\n* `translation/tests/match_errors.rs` exists with >= 12 `#[test]` functions.\n* `RUST_MIN_STACK=67108864 cargo test --offline --test match_errors -- --test-threads=1`\n  reports `0 failed`, and also passes WITHOUT `--test-threads=1`.\n* Every row of ERRORS.md sections C, D and M is covered by some test (or explicitly\n  documented as UB/unreachable in the documentation test).\n* Report: the exact final `test result:` line, the number of tests, a row-by-row\n  coverage note for sections C/D/M, and any Rust source fixes you made (with the C\n  line numbers that justified them)."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1253,"cache_read_input_tokens":292570,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1253,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f125a214-542c-4276-b4c6-bfe5147344e3","uuid":"413634d9-d8d8-499d-9302-13ac19f884fd","timestamp":"2026-09-04T05:07:22.023Z"}
