{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_clbfyf6d4aaj5uzqmetviq6x6kiabrtwv5bfcbdaayxtqijhblda","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Zero warnings, zero failures.\n\n## What was built\n\n**`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-Qil4GP/translation/tests/substitute.rs`** — 2298 lines, **22 `#[test]` functions**, built on the existing `common`/`common::diff` harness (no harness rewriting).\n\n**Final result line:**\n```\ntest result: ok. 22 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 2.63s\n```\n(stable across repeated runs; whole-crate `cargo test --offline` also fully green)\n\n### Core design\nA single driver `diff_sub_with()` runs the *same* call against both `.so`s reusing **one shared output buffer**, so the `input`/`output` pointers a substitute-callout observes are identical in both runs and can be compared as raw values. The buffer is re-filled with a `0xAA` sentinel before each run plus an 8-byte overrun guard, so every byte is *defined* — that lets it compare the **entire buffer** (a much stronger check than only the reported prefix) with no uninitialised-memory hazard, and it asserts the guard is untouched. It asserts equality of `rc`, `*outlengthptr` (on success *and* failure), all buffer bytes, and `pcre2_get_error_message` text for negative `rc`.\n\n### Coverage (~800 k differential cases ⇒ ~1.6 M `pcre2_substitute` calls, seed-fixed)\nAll 10 requested axes: full `SUBSTITUTE_*` flag matrix incl. GLOBAL combos and forwarded match options/`PARTIAL_*`; a ~180-entry replacement-syntax corpus (`$1 ${1} ${name} $name $$ $0 $& $` $' $_ $+ $<name> $*MARK`, `${n:-d}`, `${n:+a:b}` incl. 24-deep nesting vs `PTR_STACK_SIZE`, every EXTENDED escape `\\U \\L \\u \\l \\E \\Q \\n \\r \\t \\f \\a \\e \\b \\v \\0 \\x41 \\x{1F600} \\o{101} \\101 \\cA \\g<name> \\g{-1} \\1`, plus invalid forms); shapes/zero-length matches/`ZERO_TERMINATED`/startoffsets; buffer sizing incl. exact/-1/-2/0/1/huge and the two-pass workflow cross-checked against a probe; UTF & UTF|UCP with non-ASCII `\\U`/`\\L`; invalid UTF-8; named/duplicate/unset groups and small ovectors; `SUBSTITUTE_MATCHED` incl. all four `DIFFSUBS*` errors and DFA match data; a `#[repr(C)]` mirror of `pcre2_substitute_callout_block` recording and comparing the full callout sequence with returns 0/`>0`/`<0` (and \"on the Nth callout only\"); a substitute-case callout in 5 modes (ASCII, identity, always-0, ×2 expand to drive `do_case_copy`'s growth loop, and `SIZE_MAX` → `PCRE2_ERROR_REPLACECASE`), plus both callouts installed at once; 3000-iteration fuzz + 400 random-pattern fuzz.\n\n### Rust source fixes required: **none**\nNo C-vs-Rust divergence was found — `translation/src/substitute.rs` is unmodified.\n\nTo prove the suite isn't vacuous, I ran 5 mutations against `translation/src/substitute.rs`, each caught, then reverted (verified byte-identical by `diff`):\n- `pessimistic_case_inflation` `+10`→`+11` (c:292) → 2 tests fail\n- `find_text_end` `nestlevel == 0`→`<= 1` (c:102) → 3 fail\n- `*blength = buff_length + extra_needed` `+1` (c:1754) → 18 fail\n- callout-negative-return `&= !GLOBAL`→`&= !EXTENDED` (c:1673) → 1 fail\n- `$+` `group = top_bracket`→`-1` (c:1207) → 4 fail\n\n### Two cases deliberately excluded (C-side undefined behaviour, documented in-file)\n1. **Invalid UTF-8 + `PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK`** — the C library **segfaults** (e.g. subject `\"\\xff\"`, `EXTENDED|NO_UTF_CHECK`, pattern `(\\w)`/UTF). PCRE2 documents this as UB. Replaced by: invalid data *without* `NO_UTF_CHECK` (identical `UTF8_ERR*`), valid data *with* `NO_UTF_CHECK`, and invalid subjects under `PCRE2_MATCH_INVALID_UTF`.\n2. **`SUBSTITUTE_MATCHED` on a virgin match_data** — `pcre2_match_data_create` (`c_src/src/pcre2_match_data.c:53-68`) leaves `rc`, `code`, `subject`, `subject_length`, `start_offset`, `options` uninitialised; C returned `-71` from malloc garbage, Rust `-48`. Indeterminate input, not a divergence. Match data holding a real match, a recorded no-match, and a DFA match are all still tested.\n\nNote: an `ERRORS.md` appeared in `translation/` mid-session that I did not create — likely another process working in this tree. I also saw one transient whole-suite failure that did not reproduce on two subsequent runs, consistent with a concurrent rebuild of `target/release/libpcre2.so`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":395,"cache_read_input_tokens":174955,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":395,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_016TWRyfYLRynecBabLjgx9z","session_id":"f125a214-542c-4276-b4c6-bfe5147344e3","uuid":"e0fcd277-9f66-41b8-998c-f895b69a0e76","timestamp":"2026-09-04T05:09:39.178Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write substitute diff tests"}
