{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_nkejdrmw3dwuch7t5tdvcphp6sdfkmjgr6634y2dmxl6dmhce4na","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. **No divergences found in the Rust translation — zero changes were needed to `translation/src/`.**\n\n## Results\n\n**Symbol parity (Phase A/D):** 143 C exports = 143 Rust exports, 0 missing, 0 extra, 0 undefined non-libc symbols. 134 called directly by tests; the other 9 take an internal `compile_block` and are covered transitively.\n\n**184 tests, all passing** — verified stable across 5 parallel-mode runs plus a single-threaded run; `./check_features.sh` also green.\n\n| file | tests | scope |\n|---|---|---|\n| `lowlevel.rs` | 34 | `_pcre2_*_8` internals + all 27 exported data tables |\n| `match_errors.rs` | 33 | match / dfa_match / UTF error paths |\n| `compile_match.rs` | 22 | compile+match across all option axes |\n| `substitute.rs` | 22 | full substitute surface |\n| `api_errors.rs` | 19 | compile args, contexts, config, pattern_info |\n| `misc_errors.rs` | 16 | match_data, code_copy, JIT, next_match |\n| `substring.rs` / `serialize.rs` / `convert.rs` / `compile_errors.rs` / `smoke.rs` | 38 | — |\n\n**Artifacts:** `SYMBOLS.md` (143 rows), `ERRORS.md` (411), `CONFIGS.md` (260, all `[x]` with a section→test coverage map), plus `VERIFICATION.md`.\n\n## Things worth flagging\n\n**The strongest check is bytecode equality.** Every compile byte-compares the *entire* compiled program via `serialize_encode`, across ~19 000 patterns × option combinations. Allocation-failure injection additionally proved both libraries make the **identical number of heap allocations** and behave identically at every failure index.\n\n**Every failure I hit was a test defect or a table inaccuracy, never the translation.** The most instructive:\n\n- A `substring` test compared results that depend on *uninitialised* ovector slots — the C's own answer flipped between `-55` and `-1` run to run. Fixed by seeding both ovectors with the same sentinel. This only surfaced in parallel mode, which is why I ran it repeatedly rather than once.\n- **12 `ERRORS.md` rows named patterns that trigger an earlier error** than claimed. I found the real triggers by brute force and corrected the table rather than weakening the tests (e.g. `ERR35` needs `(?<=` + `(?|a|b)`×2001; `ERR84` needs `parens_nest_limit` raised or `ERR19` fires first).\n\n**Several documented inputs are genuinely UB in PCRE2's C** and are recorded, not called — I confirmed the C `.so` crashes on each, so comparing would prove nothing: `NO_UTF_CHECK` on invalid UTF-8, `DFA_RESTART` with a fresh workspace, `code_copy`/`substring_*` on a junk `code` (neither checks the magic number), and `get_hash_from_name(name, 0)` (reads `name[-1]`). For each, the well-defined neighbour *is* tested.\n\n**Non-vacuity was demonstrated by mutation:** 7 deliberate bugs seeded into `translation/src/` were each caught (1–18 test failures apiece) and reverted.\n\nOne caveat on scope: `_pcre2_jit_*` is verified only as the *defined-failure* surface this build produces, since `SUPPORT_JIT` is off — a JIT-enabled build would need separate work."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":258,"cache_read_input_tokens":467625,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":258,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f125a214-542c-4276-b4c6-bfe5147344e3","uuid":"f4b36634-5acc-4f85-9f92-cab1d3fc5e27","timestamp":"2026-09-04T05:33:20.943Z"}
